  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Noema",
      "text": "[](https://dsh-plugin.org/plugins/wjw99830/dsh-plugin-noema)\n[](https://dshfind.com/zh/plugins/wjw99830/dsh-plugin-noema?ref=badge)\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nKeep your standards in AI-assisted development\n\nNoema is a [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) plugin for developers who care about the code they ship. After each coding task, it shows complexity changes to help you decide which files and functions need a closer look"
    },
    {
      "section": "Review changes",
      "text": "Noema compares three metrics before and after each task:\n\n| Metric | What it measures |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cyclomatic complexity | Independent paths through the code |\n| Cognitive complexity | Difficulty of following control flow, accounting for branches, nesting, and recursion |\n| Maximum nesting depth | Deepest nesting of control structures within a function |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Review changes",
      "text": "Expand a file or function to locate changes within it. Its metrics include the code it contains; `[Top Level]` shows its own code separately from named child functions. Unchanged code is hidden by default and can be revealed when needed\n\nThese metrics help focus your review. Judge changes in the context of the code: a lower score alone does not mean better code"
    },
    {
      "section": "Review changes",
      "text": "Analysis runs locally and compares the workspace at the start and end of each turn, including any manual edits made during that time. Results stay outside the model context"
    },
    {
      "section": "Supported languages",
      "text": "TypeScript (including TSX), Python, and Go are supported. JavaScript and TypeScript declaration files are excluded\n\nNo card appears when there are no supported code changes, including edits limited to comments or formatting. Code changes still appear when the scores remain the same"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
